  "articleBody": "Wondering if your electrical project needs professional coordination? Here are some key signs that it's definitely time to bring in an expert. If your project includes service upgrades or any kind of panel work, that's a big signal. These tasks require specialized knowledge and adherence to strict codes. Another major indicator is if you're facing multi-trade rough-in conflicts. When electrical, plumbing, and HVAC all need to share space, a coordinator is essential to prevent clashes and costly rework. Tight inspection deadlines are another reason; professionals know the process and can ensure everything is ready on time. And, critically, if there's any work where incorrect routing or clearance could force rework or delay your occupancy, you absolutely need a licensed, coordination-savvy electrician. This isn't just about getting the job done; it's about getting it done safely and correctly the first time. HH Remodeling LLC has the experience with coordination-heavy projects and can ensure your electrical work is handled efficiently and to code, saving you stress and potential problems down the line.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}